      "translation": {
        "english_text": "Uma!... What these sweet lips play is a true yaazh; for my goal to be fulfilled... whenever I tell you anything... without asking why... without struggling to understand any reason... you must do exactly what I say!.. You must give exactly what I ask!..",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The source metaphorically calls the lips a `யாழ்` (yaazh, the classical Tamil harp); English retains the instrument name in transliteration."
        ]
      }
    },
